{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Dressing the Part", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "On-Site Interview", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 13, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Future", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you refer to future events, you can use four different tenses. Each of these tenses has their own specific use, depending on the context of the both the present and future situations. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Take a look at the chart for an outline of these tenses: ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Use\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">ll</span> have to think about it.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Be going to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"ask or talk about intentions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m going to</span> have a second interview!\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"talk about things that are arranged\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m meeting</span> the publisher and the head of web content.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"talk about schedules\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The interview <span class=\\\"strong\\\">is</span> next Thursday at 2:00 p.m.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Reported Speech and Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you are sharing information with someone about what <span class=\"underline\">someone else said or asked </span>, you can use <span class=\"strong\">reported speech</span>. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The term reported speech implies that you are reporting what someone said in the past. Therefore, when you are telling another person what someone said, you need to make the grammar structure \"more in the past\". This means that you change the verbs to a \"more past\" tense. <br> For example: <br> <span class=\"underline\">Direct</span>: <span class=\"italic\"> I <span class=\"strong\">saw</span> you at the office. <br> <span class=\"underline\">Indirect</span>: <span class=\"italic\">She said she <span class=\"strong\">had seen</span> me at the office. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you want to report questions asked, the subject normally comes before the verb.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Direct</span>: <span class=\"italic\">Why do you want to be a content editor?</span> <br><span class=\"underline\">Indirect</span>: <span class=\"italic\">They asked me why I wanted to be a web content editor.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart below for the structure of reported speech and questions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Statement/Question\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Reported Speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Why do you want to be a web content editor?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They asked me why I wanted to be a web content editor.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When are you available to start working?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Then they asked me when I was available to start working. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"What is your expected salary?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They also asked me what my expected salary was.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"How would you describe your writing style? \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They asked me how I would describe my writing style. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You should prepare some questions in advance.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They said I should prepare some questions in advance.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "on-site", "type": "name"}, {"content": "live; in person (not on the telephone or through other media)", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This on-site interview will take place at our offices at 35 Richmond Street, located at the corner of Birch Avenue. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le13ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about jobs.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "following", "type": "name"}, {"content": "after; as a result of", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(preposition)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Following your phone interview last week, it is my pleasure to invite you to a second interview at Never Odd Or Even.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le13ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word",